GO INTO MY PRESENTATION, I JUST

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:47.967
WANTED TO REITERATE THE CHAIR'S

00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.836
COMMENTS THAT OUR STATUTORY TASK

00:02:49.903 --> 00:02:51.104
AS IT RELATES TO BALLOT

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.305
MEASURES, LIMITS OUR ANALYSIS TO

00:02:52.372 --> 00:02:54.040
ONLY CONSIDERING THE FISCAL

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:56.943
ELEMENTS OF THE MEASURE, AND

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:00.013
EXPLICITLY PREVENTS US FROM

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:01.147
TALKING ABOUT THE POLICY MERITS

00:03:01.214 --> 00:03:02.215
OF THE PROPOSED CHANGE. AND

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.317
THAT'S A LITTLE BIT OF A

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.184
DIFFERENT ROLE. OR IT IS A

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.086
DIFFERENT ROLE THAN YOU'RE USED

00:03:07.153 --> 00:03:08.087
TO OF US TAKING IN THE BUDGET

00:03:08.154 --> 00:03:09.889
PROCESS WHERE WE DO WEIGH IN

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:10.924
BOTH ON THE POLICY AND FISCAL

00:03:10.990 --> 00:03:11.925
CONSIDERATIONS OF PROPOSALS. SO

00:03:11.991 --> 00:03:14.093
TO MOVE INTO THE PRESENTATION,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.128
PROP 33 IS A ESSENTIALLY A

00:03:15.194 --> 00:03:19.766
QUESTION ABOUT THE SCOPE OF

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:20.733
AUTHORITY THAT LOCAL GOVERNMENTS

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.036
IN CALIFORNIA HAVE TO ENACT RENT

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.003
CONTROL POLICIES. STATE LAW

00:03:24.070 --> 00:03:26.272
CURRENTLY ALLOWS CITIES AND

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.941
COUNTIES TO ENACT LOCAL RENT

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.909
CONTROL, BUT WITHIN CERTAIN

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:32.011
LIMITATIONS. AROUND 30

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:34.514
MUNICIPALITIES IN THE STATE HAVE

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.983
SOME FORM OF RENT CONTROL. NOW,

00:03:37.050 --> 00:03:38.184
AND THOSE ARE WITHIN THE LIMITS

00:03:38.251 --> 00:03:41.020
OF STATE LAW, WHICH ARE SET OUT

00:03:41.087 --> 00:03:42.522
IN THE COSTA-HAWKINS RENTAL

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:45.558
HOUSING ACT. THAT ACT CREATES

00:03:45.625 --> 00:03:46.559
THREE PRIMARY LIMITATIONS. THE

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:49.062
FIRST IS THAT LOCAL RENT CONTROL

00:03:49.128 --> 00:03:50.163
LAWS CANNOT APPLY TO ANY SINGLE

00:03:50.229 --> 00:03:52.899
FAMILY HOUSING. THE SECOND IS

00:03:52.966 --> 00:03:55.101
THAT IT CAN ONLY APPLY TO OLDER

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:56.269
HOUSING STOCK. IT CAN'T APPLY TO

00:03:56.336 --> 00:03:57.203
ANYTHING BUILT AFTER FEBRUARY

00:03:57.270 --> 00:03:59.939
1ST, 1995, AND THE FINAL

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:03.109
LIMITATION IS THAT A LOCAL RENT

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.177
CONTROL LAWS MUST ALLOW FOR

00:04:04.243 --> 00:04:05.878
SO-CALLED VACANCY DECONTROL, AND

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:08.815
THIS MEANS THAT THEY CAN'T TELL

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:09.949
A LANDLORD HOW MUCH THEY CAN

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.818
INCREASE RENT. WHEN THE NEW

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:12.952
RENTER IS MOVING IN. THEY'RE

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.287
LIMITED ONLY TO RESTRICTING RENT

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:17.757
INCREASES FOR EXISTING TENANTS.

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:19.759
SO SIMPLY PUT, PROP 33 WOULD

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:21.995
REPEAL COSTA-HAWKINS IN ITS

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.096
ENTIRETY. SO THIS WOULD MEAN

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.230
THERE WOULD NO LONGER BE ANY

00:04:24.297 --> 00:04:26.099
STATE LIMITATIONS ON THE TYPE

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:28.201
AND SCOPE OF RENT CONTROL THAT

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:30.003
CITIES AND COUNTIES IN THE STATE

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.571
COULD ENACT. THE MEASURE ITSELF

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:33.506
WOULDN'T MAKE ANY CHANGES TO

00:04:33.573 --> 00:04:36.275
LOCAL RENT CONTROL RULES. THOSE

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:37.243
CHANGES WOULD MOSTLY BE

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:39.946
DEPENDENT ON FUTURE ACTIONS OF

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:40.980
LOCAL ELECTED OFFICIALS AND

00:04:41.047 --> 00:04:43.449
LOCAL VOTERS. THAT BEING SAID,

00:04:43.516 --> 00:04:46.019
WE THINK BASED ON HISTORICAL

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:48.488
EXPERIENCE, IT'S LIKELY THAT

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:51.190
SOME LOCAL GOVERNMENTS WOULD

00:04:51.257 --> 00:04:52.392
EXPAND THE SCOPE OF LOCAL RENT

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.193
CONTROL TO AT LEAST SOME EXTENT

00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:57.764
OVER TIME. SO THAT LEADS TO OUR

00:04:57.830 --> 00:05:00.133
ANALYSIS OF THE MEASURES FISCAL

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:03.202
EFFECTS. ECONOMIC RESEARCH

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:04.270
SUGGESTS THAT AN EXPANSION OF

00:05:04.337 --> 00:05:05.838
LOCAL RENT CONTROL WOULD HAVE A

00:05:05.905 --> 00:05:08.675
COLLECTION OF POTENTIAL ECONOMIC

00:05:08.741 --> 00:05:09.676
EFFECTS. WE CAN'T, YOU KNOW,

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.745
GIVE A CERTAIN QUANTIFICATION OF

00:05:12.812 --> 00:05:14.714
THOSE EFFECTS BECAUSE MUCH OF IT

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:17.917
DEPENDS ON HOW MANY LOCAL

00:05:17.984 --> 00:05:18.918
GOVERNMENTS TAKE ACTION IN

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:20.086
RESPONSE TO 33. WHAT'S THE SCOPE

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:21.421
OF THOSE CHANGES? BUT WE CAN

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:22.789
DISCUSS IN GENERAL KIND OF

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:23.723
QUALITATIVELY WHAT THOSE

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:26.392
POTENTIAL EFFECTS MAY BE. AND

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:27.794
I'LL HIGHLIGHT FOUR OF THEM. TWO

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:29.629
OF THEM APPLY TO RENTERS AND TWO

00:05:29.696 --> 00:05:31.464
APPLY TO RENTAL PROPERTIES. THE

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.632
FIRST FOR RENTERS IS THAT SOME

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:36.069
COULD FACE A CHANGE IN THE COST

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:38.037
THEY PAY FOR RENT. ON THE ONE

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:38.838
HAND, SOME RENTERS, SPECIFICALLY

00:05:38.905 --> 00:05:41.107
THOSE WHO LIVE IN RENTALS THAT

00:05:41.174 --> 00:05:42.308
ARE NEWLY COVERED BY AN EXPANDED

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:44.177
RENT CONTROL RULE, LIKELY WOULD

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:45.344
PAY LESS FOR RENT THAN THEY

00:05:45.411 --> 00:05:46.913
OTHERWISE WOULD. ON THE OTHER

00:05:46.979 --> 00:05:49.816
HAND, OTHER RENTERS COULD END UP

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.851
PAYING MORE FOR RENT. AN EXAMPLE

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.119
THIS COULD BE A RENTER THAT IS

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:55.455
LIVING IN A NEIGHBORING

00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:58.057
MUNICIPALITY TO A ONE THAT JUST

00:05:58.124 --> 00:05:59.992
EXPANDED RENT CONTROL, BUT WHERE

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:01.894
THERE IS NOT A RENT CONTROL IN

00:06:01.961 --> 00:06:03.796
THE MUNICIPALITY THAT THEY'RE

00:06:03.863 --> 00:06:05.932
LIVING. THE SECOND POTENTIAL

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:09.102
EFFECT ON RENTERS IS THAT THEY

00:06:09.168 --> 00:06:10.303
WOULD TEND TO MOVE LESS OFTEN,

00:06:10.369 --> 00:06:11.704
AND THIS CAN BE FOR A FEW

00:06:11.771 --> 00:06:15.308
REASONS. ONE IS SOME RENTERS MAY

00:06:15.374 --> 00:06:16.576
BE LESS LIKELY TO ESSENTIALLY BE

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:18.311
SORT OF FORCED TO MOVE BECAUSE

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.378
THEY CAN'T AFFORD A RENT

00:06:19.445 --> 00:06:21.380
INCREASE. ALSO, YOU COULD HAVE

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:22.515
SOME RENTERS WHO SIMPLY CHOOSE

00:06:22.582 --> 00:06:24.584
NOT TO MOVE BECAUSE THEY ARE

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.419
RECEIVING A GOOD DEAL ON THEIR

00:06:26.486 --> 00:06:28.387
RENT CONTROLLED APARTMENT AND DO

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.590
NOT WANT TO PAY MORE TO MOVE TO

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.525
A NEW RENTAL. SO THOSE ARE KIND

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:34.861
OF THE EFFECTS. THE Kò EFFECTS

00:06:34.927 --> 00:06:36.028
ON RENTERS MOVING TO RENTAL

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:37.797
PROPERTIES THEMSELVES. THE FIRST

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:40.500
Kò EFFECT IS A LIKELY REDUCTION

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:41.667
IN THE SUPPLY OF RENTAL HOUSING,

00:06:41.734 --> 00:06:43.469
AND THERE'S A FEW POTENTIAL

00:06:43.536 --> 00:06:45.805
MECHANISMS FOR THIS. THE ONE FOR

00:06:45.872 --> 00:06:48.441
WHICH THERE'S THE MOST EVIDENCE

00:06:48.508 --> 00:06:49.542
IS THAT LANDLORDS WOULD SOME

00:06:49.609 --> 00:06:51.410
LANDLORDS WOULD ESSENTIALLY GET

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:53.179
OUT OF THE BUSINESS OF BEING A

00:06:53.246 --> 00:06:53.780
LANDLORD. THEY WOULD SELL THE

00:06:53.846 --> 00:06:57.083
RENTAL TO SOMEONE, AN OWNER WHO

00:06:57.150 --> 00:06:58.217
WOULD LIVE THERE. THEY WOULD

00:06:58.284 --> 00:07:00.086
CONVERT IT TO A CONDO, ETC. THIS

00:07:00.153 --> 00:07:01.888
WOULD REDUCE THE NUMBER OF

00:07:01.954 --> 00:07:03.156
RENTALS THAT ARE AVAILABLE FOR

00:07:03.222 --> 00:07:06.058
RENTERS. THE FINAL EFFECT IS

00:07:06.125 --> 00:07:09.162
THAT RENTAL HOUSING WOULD LIKELY

00:07:09.228 --> 00:07:10.196
BECOME LESS PROFITABLE, AND THIS

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:13.032
WOULD REDUCE THE AMOUNT THAT

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:14.033
POTENTIAL LANDLORDS ARE WILLING

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:15.101
TO PAY FOR RENTAL PROPERTIES,

00:07:15.168 --> 00:07:17.570
REDUCING THE VALUE OF THOSE

00:07:17.637 --> 00:07:21.240
PROPERTIES. SO NARROWING IN FROM

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:22.775
THESE ECONOMIC EFFECTS, WE CAN

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:27.046
TALK ABOUT A FEW KIND OF

00:07:27.113 --> 00:07:28.014
SPECIFIC EFFECTS THAT THE

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:29.248
MEASURE COULD HAVE ON THE

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:32.185
FINANCES OF STATE AND LOCAL

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:33.820
GOVERNMENTS. AND I'LL HIGHLIGHT

00:07:33.886 --> 00:07:34.987
TWO Kò KIND OF FISCAL EFFECTS.

00:07:35.054 --> 00:07:37.523
THE FIRST AND MOST SIGNIFICANT

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.325
IS A LIKELY REDUCTION IN

00:07:39.392 --> 00:07:41.928
PROPERTY TAX REVENUES FOR LOCAL

00:07:41.994 --> 00:07:42.929
GOVERNMENTS AND SCHOOLS. AND

00:07:42.995 --> 00:07:45.198
THIS KIND OF FLOWS DIRECTLY FROM

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.299
THE ECONOMIC IMPACT. I MENTIONED

00:07:46.365 --> 00:07:49.535
A MINUTE AGO ABOUT A REDUCTION

00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:50.870
IN THE VALUE OF RENTAL

00:07:50.937 --> 00:07:52.171
PROPERTIES. WE THINK THAT THAT

00:07:52.238 --> 00:07:53.739
REDUCTION IN PROPERTY TAXES OVER

00:07:53.806 --> 00:07:55.541
TIME COULD REACH AT LEAST TENS

00:07:55.608 --> 00:07:57.877
OF MILLIONS OF DOLLARS PER YEAR.

00:07:57.944 --> 00:08:00.913
THE OTHER FISCAL EFFECT IS A

00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:02.481
LIKELY INCREASE IN

00:08:02.548 --> 00:08:03.482
ADMINISTRATIVE COSTS FOR LOCAL

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:05.384
GOVERNMENTS TO CARRY OUT

00:08:05.451 --> 00:08:08.321
EXPANDED RENT CONTROL RULES.

00:08:08.387 --> 00:08:09.422
THOSE COSTS COULD BE IN THE

00:08:09.488 --> 00:08:11.290
MILLIONS OF DOLLARS A YEAR, UP

00:08:11.357 --> 00:08:13.125
TO TENS OF MILLIONS OF DOLLARS,

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:14.293
AND TRADITIONALLY THOSE COSTS

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.363
ARE PAID BY FEES THAT ARE LEVIED

00:08:17.430 --> 00:08:20.600
ON LANDLORDS. SO WITH THAT, I

00:08:20.666 --> 00:08:22.335
WILL BE HAPPY TO TAKE ANY

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:24.337
QUESTIONS. THANK YOU VERY MUCH

00:08:24.403 --> 00:08:25.671
FOR THAT. OVERVIEW. MEMBERS.

00:08:25.738 --> 00:08:28.307
QUESTIONS. YES, SENATOR RUSSELL,

00:08:28.374 --> 00:08:30.776
GO AHEAD. THANK YOU. THANK YOU

00:08:30.843 --> 00:08:35.348
FOR YOUR REPORT. WHEN YOU SAID

00:08:35.414 --> 00:08:39.318
THAT THERE WOULD, IN TERMS OF

00:08:39.385 --> 00:08:41.153
THE FISCAL IMPACT ON LOCAL

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.188
GOVERNMENTS OR ANYWHERE IN THE

00:08:42.255 --> 00:08:46.859
STATE, LIKE THEY WOULD BE LESS

00:08:46.926 --> 00:08:47.860
PROFITABLE, LANDLORDS WOULD SELL

00:08:47.927 --> 00:08:49.762
PROPERTIES. WHAT DO YOU BASING

00:08:49.829 --> 00:08:53.199
THAT ON? AND DID YOU BASE IT ON

